{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>These shall stand.</b> All those who stood for the blessing were sons of the mistresses, and since the sons of Leah were numerous, they took from them both the small and the great to complete the count, over against the sons of the maidservants who were only four. And they were on the curse the great and the small — the great is Reuben, because he was suspect in the matter of Bilhah, and he answered Amen to 'cursed be he who lies with his father's wife,' and his father surely knew that he had not transgressed in this matter. And thus it is stated in chapter במה בהמה יוצאה: perhaps his seed is destined to stand on Mount Eival and say, 'cursed be he who lies with his father's wife,' and this sin will come upon him. And the small is Zevulun." "<b>To bless the people.</b> Rashi explained: six tribes went up etc. That is according to the Mishnah of 'ואלו נאמרין' (and these are said), but Rabbi says: both these and those — Israelites and Levites — stand below, as it is written in the book of Joshua: 'וכל ישראל וזקניו ושופטיו והכהנים והלוים עומדים מזה ומזה לארון' etc. And what is written in the portion Re'eh — 'on Mount Gerizim and on Mount Eival' — that means adjacent, as it is written 'וסכות על הארון' (and you shall spread over the ark). It was taught: Rabbi Eliezer says: one cannot say Levi is below, for it was already stated that Levi is above — 'these shall stand to bless the people on Mount Gerizim: Shimon and Levi and Yehudah'; and one cannot say Levi is above, for it was already stated in Joshua: 'וכל ישראל וזקניו' etc. 'והכהנים והלוים עומדים מזה ומזה לארון' — how so? Elders of priesthood and Levites below, and the rest above. Rabbi Yehoshua says: all who are fit for service to carry the ark, that is, from age thirty to age fifty — below, next to the ark, and the rest above. Rashi further explained here: they opened with the blessing, 'ברוך האיש' etc., and the proof is from Joshua: 'half of them toward Mount Gerizim and half of them toward Mount Eival, as Moses the servant of HaShem commanded לברך את עם ישראל בראשונה.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:31.429635159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}